{"abstract":"Temperature has strong potential to mediate emotion in a range of contexts; augmenting sensory experience and/or supporting emotion regulation. Hence, there is growing interest in leveraging thermal cues for affective technologies. At present, however, the design space for thermal technologies for emotion regulation remains underexplored and largely undefined. We construct a design space for thermal affective emotion regulation technologies, clarifying the rich, expressive nature of thermal cues as a design material. We develop this through a Research through Design (RtD) approach, grounded in an 18-month autoethnographic inquiry based on the first author’s emotion regulation practice. We contribute a structured design space for thermal affective interaction, linking experience and design implementation with designerly know-how. By discussing the creation of this design space we provide insights into the generative process of developing intermediate-level knowledge from autoethnographic study and design practice.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Feng, Feng","Halskov, Kim","Bennett, Daniel Thomas","Pakanen, Minna","Mekler, Elisa D."],"cuid":["S02-092.11-832088"],"filters":{"added":"2026-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bristol"],"keyword":["Autoethnography","Design space","Emotion regulation","Research through Design","Sensory modality","Temperature","Thermal"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"constructing the thermal affective design space for emotion regulation an autoethnographic research through design inquiry","src":["aau","au"],"src-code"