{"abstract":"Thermal-afective experience is a growing topic in Human-Computer Interaction. However, research linking thermal and afective experience in technology use has not moved beyond attempts to establish broad, sweeping associations, such as between warmth and positive afect. One of the obstacles to progression is the need for frameworks and vocabularies that describe and conceptualise the richness of thermal perception and afective experience. To help conceptualise associations between thermal perception and afective experience we turn to Cí poetry, a form of classical Chinese literature rich with evocative descriptions of embodied, environmentally situated, frst-person experience. We conducted a lexical analysis to identify thermal-afective associations, and propose a design framework addressing thermal design. We demonstrate the value of this framework via analysis of existing thermal design exemplars.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Feng, Feng","Bennett, Daniel","Mekler, Elisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747222"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cross cultural","Design","Emotion","Framework","Lexicon","Multisensory","Thermal","Translation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"smiles summon the warmth of spring a framework for thermal and affective design grounded in classical chinese poetry","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661620","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747222","identifier":[{"id":"85200394791","t